  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Assistance with the Administration of Applications for Temporary Protection in Ireland</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Built on the experience of the Project &#x201C;Registration of Ukrainian Nationals and TCNs entering Ireland&#x201D; started in March 2022 of the initial duration of 12 months and further extended until 31.10.23, the current project proposal aims to continue to further support the Department of Justice of the Government of Ireland with the registration and administration of the TP applications of the Ukrainian nationals and TCNs entering Ireland. In continuation of the current Registration of Ukrainian nationals and TCNs in Ireland Project, IOM will deploy a pool of approximately 20 skilled Ukrainian and Russian speaking staff, in the following duty stations: Dublin Airport, Dublin Citywest, Limerick, Cork and Rosslare Europort. This will be done in order to ensure that the responsible authorities in Ireland will continue to be assisted by a high standard of specialized personnel, be able to deal with migratory pressure for the country in a comprehensive border governance approach and consolidate the best practices developed since March 2022.</narrative>
  </description>
